{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side","id":1190888,"title":"[Doubt] stepping sideways: No room to occupy on the other side","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-01T19:50:01-08:00","id":1190888,"title":"[Doubt] stepping sideways: No room to occupy on the other side","content":"When a garou attempts to reach the umbra (or vise-versa), but there is no occupable territory. How to proceed?<br /> <br /> <b>For example: </b><br /> <br /> 1. A garou in a underground installation, like a military base, try to reach penumbra, but in penumbra have no path, only solid ground.<br /> 2. A garou in a penumbra cave, try to reach physical world, but in physical world the correspondence is opaque concrete. <br /> <br /> <b>What does the narrator do? </b><br /> <br /> -Close Guantlet?<br /> -The Garou reach, but not pass? <br /> -He pass, but gets stuck in the obstacle?<br /> -He reach in another location near?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T20:57:28-08:00","id":1190900,"title":"","content":"Example 1: Assume that the Penumbra has the same general layout. If there's a subterranean installation, it will have a corresponding Penumbral landscape with open tunnels.<br /> Example 2: I'm having a bit of a difficult time imagining the context here. Did someone pour concrete into an entire cave system? The entrance? If so, there should be an indicator on the other side, because that's going to be a rather large change.<br /> <br /> If in doubt, you can have a character in the pack peak through the Gauntlet in order to discern how different things are. Make sure to remind the players of this, and don't feel the need to be too subtle about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:58:20-08:00","id":1190927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1190900#post1190900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example 1: Assume that the Penumbra has the same general layout. If there's a subterranean installation, it will have a corresponding Penumbral landscape with open tunnels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember that it takes about a hundred years for an object in the physical plane to get a corresponding Penumbral reflection, unless it's spiritually significant in some way. One minor plot I've got going is I've got a military unit (that knows about the Penumbra) that intentionally sited a holding cell for Garou below grade specifically to short-circuit their &quot;disappearing-into-thin-air trick&quot;. I sort of always assumed that any attempt to step sideways into solid rock simply fails regardless of the number of successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:35:24-08:00","id":1190962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1190900#post1190900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example 1: Assume that the Penumbra has the same general layout. If there's a subterranean installation, it will have a corresponding Penumbral landscape with open tunnels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try to imagine a newly built basement in a house, it does not yet have penumbral representation. In the penumbra, the same location (the basement), there is only solid rock. <br /> <br /> Let's think now:<br /> <br /> -If a garou try to reaches the penumbra inside the basement. What happens?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:51:47-08:00","id":1190964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1190927#post1190927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember that it takes about a hundred years for an object in the physical plane to get a corresponding Penumbral reflection, unless it's spiritually significant in some way. One minor plot I've got going is I've got a military unit (that knows about the Penumbra) that intentionally sited a holding cell for Garou below grade specifically to short-circuit their &quot;disappearing-into-thin-air trick&quot;. I sort of always assumed that any attempt to step sideways into solid rock simply fails regardless of the number of successes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. But I've never seen any official book clarifying this issue. <br /> I remember when I was curious about the landscape of the moon bridge. The only place I found anything about was in the book Rite of Passage (1992).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T11:16:22-08:00","id":1191051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baskin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1190962#post1190962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try to imagine a newly built basement in a house, it does not yet have penumbral representation. In the penumbra, the same location (the basement), there is only solid rock.<br /> <br /> Let's think now:<br /> <br /> -If a garou try to reaches the penumbra inside the basement. What happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with the same thing. If you dig down into the earth, it changes in the Penumbra, too, so as to cut down on headaches. It's not really much of a stretch when it comes to lore, since...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I seem to remember that it takes about a hundred years for an object in the physical plane to get a corresponding Penumbral reflection, unless it's spiritually significant in some way. One minor plot I've got going is I've got a military unit (that knows about the Penumbra) that intentionally sited a holding cell for Garou below grade specifically to short-circuit their &quot;disappearing-into-thin-air trick&quot;. I sort of always assumed that any attempt to step sideways into solid rock simply fails regardless of the number of successes.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Writing kind of forced the issue to be a bit faster with this in some cases. DNA had an escapee use this method of egress, and said escapee didn't end up eating rock or trying and coming up with nothing. The presence of a Garou or Fera in the locales might have had something to do with it, but it's a trend that other writing took on as well, including the SF0 section of Demon Hunter X.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T16:43:48-08:00","id":1191160,"title":"","content":"Stepping sideways is basically like opening a door to another dimension/world. If where the door opens is somewhere that is impassable to you, then despite the door being open you can't cross over.<br /> <br /> In terms of flavor text, I would probably rule that it is somewhat similar to being &quot;stuck&quot; between worlds except that you can immediately cross back to the world where you came from.<br /> <br /> Then just move to a different location and try again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T04:33:44-08:00","id":1191888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1191160#post1191160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepping sideways is basically like opening a door to another dimension/world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it?<br /> The 2nd Edition intro comic shows it like that, but rules don't describe it like that.<br /> <br /> I would handle it like this:<br /> If you have a basement in the material world, there is one in the penumbra, too. Periode. If there wasn't it would be as if the basment would have no soul, and that doesn't make sense, since the existence of the basement isn't disputed.<br /> Now, of course people would say that RAW, changes to the material world need time to take effect in the penumbra. I agree, however, there was no change to the basement, it was newly created. The change in question was made to the penumbral representation of the street, where the new house and it's basement were build. If a garou stepped sideways in the street, house and basement weren't present and therefor not accessible. But if the garou was in the house, the house, and it's basement would have it's own part of the penumbra. And sure, that would mean that a garou could walk out of the penumbral representation of the new house into the representation of the street, turn around and by unable to walk back, for there wasn't the house behind him anymore. But, the umbra doesn't have to adhere to normal physics like distances, geometry or such.<br /> <br /> Question 2:<br /> If the penumbra was altered in a significant way, like digging a cave like hole, that was not present in the material world. I wouldn't allow to step outside for any character who was aware of the fact. So it would be like reaching but not initiating the trasition. People who don't know about this problem, I would allow them to stepp sideways appearing on the nearest reasonable place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:17:08-08:00","id":1193032,"title":"","content":"I would also argue that tearing through the earth to creat a basement/underground facility is a big enough disturbance to the spirit world to have an almost immediate correspondence in the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:29:24-08:00","id":1193037,"title":"","content":"Otherwise I would just say that the gauntlet is simply to thick to even attempt crossing over. <br /> I'm also not sure if something like earth layers even exists in the Umbra, since it is not a realm of physicality and matter but of abstract representation of the conceptual and ephemeral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23979-traldar","name":"Traldar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:24:35-08:00","id":1193101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traldar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1193037#post1193037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise I would just say that the gauntlet is simply to thick to even attempt crossing over.<br /> I'm also not sure if something like earth layers even exists in the Umbra, since it is not a realm of physicality and matter but of abstract representation of the conceptual and ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exist in Penumbra, the shadow of the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:15:50-08:00","id":1193212,"title":"","content":"There was rules for City Penumbra in 2002 Book of the City, they were about high floors... AFAIR in 30-65% of situations you wouldn't find penumbral floor and will fall. I don't see why the same logic isn't appropriate to the underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10938-jargal","name":"Jargal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:21:06-08:00","id":1193282,"title":"","content":"In the case of the basement in a house, that's a weaverish disturbance, and would take some time to develop a presence in the penumbra. In my opinion, if a Garou tried to step sideways from inside the basement of a new house, he'd find his passage through to the other side of the gauntlet blocked by dirt or rock or whatever was removed to make space for the basement. Imagine opening a door only to see a wall on the other side. Like this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://l7.alamy.com/zooms/12284414b5614b9c8e06f6769fdeaa51/door-in-brick-wall-leading-to-nowhere-by124a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T02:50:46-08:00","id":1193475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jargal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1193212#post1193212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was rules for City Penumbra in 2002 Book of the City, they were about high floors... AFAIR in 30-65% of situations you wouldn't find penumbral floor and will fall. I don't see why the same logic isn't appropriate to the underground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found this passage kind of unfortunate for the flow of the game and constraining in case of the Setting as a whole.<br /> <br /> If I run a plot, and for some reason the PCs decide to step onto the Penumbra, be it an informed decision or a stupid idea, I don't want the whole affair to drag out and leave a rat's tail on secondary elements in the process. Like, can I do it here, or do I need to leave the building? If this floor is possibly not yet in the Penumbra, do I need to go to ground floor or get out on the street, is 3rd flore maybe far enough down? How will this affect the overall quest, in terms of people who might see the PCs and how they will react doe to the Curse? If we have to leave the building to enter the penumbra outside, all gifts are deavtivated, for that is for sure a new scene, right?<br /> <br /> That is just bad for the flow of any story. Also, metaphysically it doesn't make sense to be, as described above. The Umbra is multilayered. There is the Astral Plane's Penumbra part (which Werewolves could only access with a Stargazer gift) that shows the characters opinions and believes reflected back on the character. Then there is the Shadowlands, the Dark Umbra's Penumbra part, which shows everything's hidden decay and death. There is the Chimerical, which is kind of the Dreaming's Penumbra (although it isn't a world of it's own), showing the phantasies of people. And lastly the Middle Umbra's Penumbra, the one that werewolves interact with, which is the Soul of the material world, as is.<br /> <br /> So, if one is in a high rise's 40th floor, this part of the physical world should have a soul, just like any part on the ground or an airplane. Sure, if you are on a street in old town, where one street side was demolished and replaced with said highrise, you might if you step into the penumbra not see this highrise, because in the soul of the world, this new installment has no place yet. However, Umbra isn't necessary physically stable space. So, while someone stepping into the street's penumbra outside the building might not see it, someone in the building stepping into the building's penumbra, might still be in the building.<br /> <br /> The assuption here is that every thing has a penumbra. The penumbra is not a 1:1 copy of the material world, but has overlapping areas. This suits the game imo better, since you can allow to step sideways anywhere, but you still maintain that change is slowly added to the penumbra. However, new places or moveable areas like ships and planes are no places of 2n class, always lacking penumbra represrentation because they are mobile. I mean, a aircraft carrier is basically it's own city. That is moves should not deny a penumbra representation. The orient express, full of legends...<br /> <br /> ...and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:28:34-08:00","id":1193516,"title":"","content":"I think I understand your logic, but one thing interest me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1193475#post1193475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, while someone stepping into the street's penumbra outside the building might not see it, someone in the building stepping into the building's penumbra, might still be in the building.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they step aside at the same time, what a character who stands on the ground sees - umbral building suddenly appeared where it never was? Or other character float in the air?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10938-jargal","name":"Jargal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:20:25-08:00","id":1193592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1193282#post1193282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of the basement in a house, that's a weaverish disturbance, and would take some time to develop a presence in the penumbra. In my opinion, if a Garou tried to step sideways from inside the basement of a new house, he'd find his passage through to the other side of the gauntlet blocked by dirt or rock or whatever was removed to make space for the basement. Imagine opening a door only to see a wall on the other side. Like this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea. Preserve the tone of the game and the mood of mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","user":"Baskin","date":". 03-09-2018, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T07:28:41-07:00","id":1194528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jargal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1190888-doubt-stepping-sideways-no-room-to-occupy-on-the-other-side?p=1193516#post1193516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they step aside at the same time, what a character who stands on the ground sees - umbral building suddenly appeared where it never was? Or other character float in the air?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure, what you are asking, but elaboration on the scenario more:<br /> <br /> The character who would be on the street is character A. He is in a different scene then character B, who is in the newly build building. Both scenes run simultaniously. Both stepp sideways. Character A is in the penumbra of the street. Character B is in the penumbra of the building, specifically the room he was on. Character A wouldn' be able to see what charackter A does, for the penumbra of the house is a adjacent part of penumbral reality. Character B would be able to look out of a window and see either the penumbral equivalent of the street the building is build on in the material world OR just A near umbral representation the concept of 'a neighbourhood street'. Wits+Enigmas might allow him to discern the difference. If it is the former, character B might be able to see character A, with variing detail. Which ever is true, depends on the situation, see later.<br /> <br /> So, what can happen:<br /> 1. Character B leaves the building for the penumbral equivalent of the actual street the building is on. Character A would see/hear/smell a translucent version of character B appear and solidify, as he moves from the on slice of penumbra to the other.<br /> 2. Charakter A knows that there is a newly build house in the material world he can't see in his penumbral street. He wants to enter it anyway, but not by stepping back into the matieral, enter the building and step back into the penumbra. So, he (or al least on person of his group, if he is with others) starts Peeking. This grounds him to the material world. He is now able to walk into the penumbral equivalent of the building, that is not yet part of the penumbra of the adjacent street. For other observers from A's former position, it would look like as if he would fade away while moving.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, when to choose what way on how different slices of penumbra border to each other ot the near umbra?<br /> Well, make it a way most people would expect, with penumbra being adjacent to penumbra and people who can see into the adjacent slice of penumbra in all cases where I want the pack to find each other again quickly, for example when building up to an action sequence.<br /> <br /> I would use the other method if the pack is investigating and I want to build up or perserve a feeling of wonder and the unexpected. Meaning in all cases I use the fact that distances, illumination, sound distortion and dampening and all that is not bound by physical constrains in the Penumbra (or passages to the Near Umbra) - it is so to make the players feel eerie<br /> <br /> However. It is necessary that you always appear to have a plan on how the physics of the situation work, so that Players feel like, they could figure it out. You shouldn't frustrate the players with telling them something is unexpected, seemingly on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}